course: dictionary
lesson: 12346
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «Dad had to crank the handle before the old car would start.» Here crank is a verb, and the handle is turned round and round to make a machine work.
explain: «Ben's uncle is a crank who believes the Earth is flat, and he will not listen to the science.» A crank here is a person, not a handle. The clue is «will not listen»: a crank has strange ideas and will not change them.
explain: Some words are joined to a second word to make a new meaning. «Turn the music up and crank it up!» Crank up means to turn up the volume, the heat or the power. Look for the little word next to the main word, such as up or out, because it often changes the meaning.
fact: Crank can be a noun (a thing or a person) or a verb (an action).
fact: «Crank» as a noun can mean a handle bent at a right angle, which is used to make a machine work.
fact: «Crank» can mean a person with strange, fixed ideas, or in US slang, a grumpy person.
fact: «Crank up» means to turn up the volume, heat or power, and «crank out» means to produce lots of things quickly.
fact: A «crank call» is a prank phone call, and in science a crank can turn spinning movement into back-and-forth movement, like pedals on a bicycle.
exercise: «The old car would not start, so Mum had to crank the handle at the front.» What does crank mean here? | To paint the car a bright colour | *To turn a handle round and round to start a machine | To stop the engine with a loud bang
exercise: «Ben's uncle is a crank who believes the Earth is flat, and he will not listen to the science.» What is a crank in this sentence? | A loud, happy singer | *A person with strange, fixed ideas who will not listen | A bicycle pedal
exercise: «Turn the radio up. Crank up the music!» What does crank up mean? | *Turn up the volume | Fall asleep on the sofa | Turn off the lights
test: «The factory can crank out a hundred toys an hour.» What does crank out mean? | *Make lots of things quickly | Sell every toy at the shop | Lose things slowly | Stop the machines for a rest
test: «The phone rang, and it was a crank call from a boy playing a joke.» What is a crank call? | A call from a grandparent far away | *A prank phone call | A call to the fire station for help
exam: On a bicycle, the cranks are | *The arms the pedals are fixed to, which turn round and round | The seat where you sit | The bell that you ring to warn people | The brakes that stop the wheels
